# CI etiquette (CSL-255)

- Open pull requests as **drafts**.
- **Batch pushes.** Prefer one push per iteration; do not push every local commit.
- Mark a PR **ready once**, only after validation and when no owner hold remains. An owner request to keep a PR draft takes precedence; do not flip draft ↔ ready repeatedly.
- Never merge a PR. Do not routinely merge the base into a working branch. A normal base merge is allowed only for a **real conflict** or an **owner-approved dependency integration**, even when that integration has no text conflict; record the reason and rerun the combined gates. Never rebase or force-push.
- Never edit `.github/workflows/**` unless a Linear issue explicitly assigned by a human asks for it.
- Bots mark a PR ready with **their own identity**, never `GITHUB_TOKEN`.
